    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-mīrus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>very wonderful</i>
			 (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut mihi permirum videatur, quemquam exstare,
					etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 47, 99</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illud vero mihi permirum accidit, fuisse, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 3, 10, 5</span></i>
			.—In tmesi: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per mihi mirum visum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 1, 49, 214</span></i>
			.</div>
